## Installation

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## Run

```bash
alembic upgrade head
uvicorn {{ package_name }}.main:app --reload
```

The API documentation is available at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs` and the
health endpoint at `http://127.0.0.1:8000{{ health_path }}`.

Collection endpoints are paginated with `page` and `page_size` query parameters.
Pages start at `1`, the default page size is `20`, and the maximum is `100`.
Responses contain `items`, `page`, `page_size`, `total`, and `pages`.

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` to customize the service. Configuration uses
the `APP_` prefix, including `APP_DATABASE_URL`, `APP_DEBUG`, and
`APP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`. SQLite is used by default.

## Database migrations

The initial schema is managed by Alembic. After changing the ORM models, create
and apply a new migration:

```bash
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the schema change"
alembic upgrade head
```

To revert the latest migration, run `alembic downgrade -1`. Application startup
does not create or modify database tables automatically.

